WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.200
hey everyone today we're setting up dual WAN failover on pfSense

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:09.100
dual WAN failover on pfSense with a fiber line and a Starlink backup

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:15.800
the box is a Protectli VP2420 running pfSense Plus 24.11

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:08.500
first go to System, Routing, Gateways and add the Starlink gateway

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:14.000
set the monitor IP to 1.1.1.1 so it's not pinging the Starlink dish itself

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:37.400
now under System, Routing, Gateway Groups make a group called WAN_FAILOVER

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:44.900
fiber is tier one, Starlink is tier two, trigger level member down

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:16.200
and I set pool options to round robin with sticky address on the group

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:12.000
then in Firewall, Rules, LAN edit the default allow rule, advanced options, and set the gateway to WAN_FAILOVER

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:26.000
last thing under System, Advanced, Miscellaneous tick flush all states when a gateway goes down

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:05.000
you can see here on the gateway group page the pool options field

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:46.000
pull the fiber and within about ten seconds traffic is on Starlink
